        "operational",
        "oversight",
        "intelligence"
      ],
      "assurance_summary": "Availability: services run in three UK regions; when one region fails the other two keep a majority and continue, and data is replicated between regions. Confidentiality: users must authenticate (OIDC, MFA, short-lived tokens) and the policy engine grants access only when the access-control matrix, Bell-LaPadula and Biba all permit; datastores are encrypted, and five trust boundaries separate users, the operational, intelligence and oversight domains, and research partners. Integrity: critical transactions commit only with agreement from a majority of replicas (Raft, Paxos), and BFT protects the audit log and intelligence against tampering by up to f malicious validators. Replication cannot protect against common-mode failures (supply chain, pre-commit corruption), which remain the principal residual risks."
    },
